                  <msItem>
                     <title>Cicero, Rhetorica; etc.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">(fols. 121r--133r) do not quite certainly
                        belong with the rest.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">For E. de T. cf. Oriel Coll. 4, Auct, F.v.28
                        (from Oriel), Lambeth Palace 1106 nad Oriel Coll. Records. He was fellow of
                        Oriel c. 1350--1360, see Richards and Shadwell, The provosts and fellows of
                        Oriel College, Oxford (Oxford 1922), p. 8. The inscr. on fol. 134v is in the
                        same hand as that in Lambeth 1106, and as the inscr. 'per m. Eliam de
                        Trikyngham' in Oriel Coll. 4 (which has also in another hand 'liber domus
                        beate Marie de Oryell per m. Helyam de Trykyngham').</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
